# Files that run inside Linux (bash, make, docker build) keep LF line endings on
# every OS. Git for Windows checks text out with CRLF by default
# (core.autocrlf=true), and a CRLF scan.sh then fails on its first command:
#   scan.sh: line 3: set: -: invalid option
# Only these patterns are listed on purpose: every other file keeps Git's
# default handling, so nothing else in the tree changes bytes.
*.sh          text eol=lf
Makefile      text eol=lf
Dockerfile    text eol=lf
Dockerfile.*  text eol=lf
